  "answer": "Project Zenith is a new data analytics initiative launched on June 15th with a $500,000 budget for phase one, led by Sarah Tan. The project aims to revolutionize data analytics using AI. Key milestones and updates include: an initial findings report in August highlighting a potential 20% efficiency increase; a call for R&D ideas by July 20th to enhance data visualization; the approval of a $15,000 training budget for coding teams and project managers; a celebration of the testing phase completion on October 10th; a phase two progress update in November regarding breakthroughs in predictive analytics; and ongoing efforts to secure strategic partnerships with TechInnovate for AI technology. Additionally, feedback is being sought from stakeholders on the prototype's performance and user experience by the end of November."
